    "title": "Bill Murray supporting UConn men at NCAA Final Four",
    "text": "Actor Bill Murray looks on prior to a game between the UConn Huskies and the Duke Blue Devils in the Elite Eight of the 2026 NCAA Men's Basketball Tournament at Capital One Arena on March 29, 2026 in Washington, DC. Murray, father of UConn assistant coach Luke Murray, was also at the Final Four game vs. Illinois on April 4, 2026.Patrick Smith/Getty ImagesSaturday's Final Four matchup between UConn men's basketball and Illinois places legendary actor Bill Murray at a very cinematic crossroads, forced to choose between his Illini roots and his family.Murray was born and raised in Evanston, Ill. and grew up as a fan of the Fighting Illini, although he elected to briefly attend Regis University in Denver before sparking his comedic acting career. However, his son, Luke Murray, has served as an assistant for UConn over the past five seasons, reaching his third Final Four with head coach Dan Hurley's program this weekend.Article continues below this adGet Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.Get Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.ONLY 25¢The Huskies have stolen Murray's hometown allegiances ahead of Saturday's Final Four clash, as the 75-year-old actor confirmed to the Chicago Tribune that he will be rooting for UConn. Murray's about-face is more practical than sentimental, joking that his UConn loyalty ensures him tickets to UConn NCAA Tournament games.“I only get tickets if I keep my mouth shut,” he wrote in a text to the Chicago Tribune.Illinois is making its first Final Four appearance in more than two decades after outlasting Big Ten rivals Iowa to reach the national semifinal stage. During the Illini's last run in 2005, Murray was one of the school's most prominent supporters, both for his more contemporary film success and an iconic outfit that included an orange tie.Article continues below this adLuke Murray has been hired as the Boston College head coach and is coaching his final weekend with the Huskies. The Fairfield graduate has been a crucial part of Hurley's staff at UConn as the architect of the Huskies' offense.Make CT Insider a preferred source on Google to see more of our journalism when you search.Add Preferred SourceBill Murray has been a constant presence throughout his coaching rise through the coaching ranks, attending games at Wagner, Rhode Island, Xavier and Louisville while Luke coached at those spots. He has been visible at UConn postseason games during the team's title runs.Article continues below this adGet daily updates from the UConn basketball world.",
